`scripts/llm-serve` is a bash control script (start/stop/switch/status/restart/logs) for a local Qwen LLM stack — it launches either `llama-server` (GGUF) or `mlx_vlm.server` (MLX) with benchmarked MTP speculative-decoding and prompt-caching settings, plus an Anthropic-API proxy (`llm-proxy.mjs`) in front, and handles orphan-process recovery, port-waiting, and disk-cache management.
